            "review_text": "Minh-Anh Quach\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam166 contributions\n0\nDecent noodles, pass the tempura\nOct 2017 • Couples\nLocal Vietnamese, few tourists and even Japanese were there when I went to try this place. The broth of the dishes was tasty, not wowing, good enough to satisfy an udon craving. You can add many spices (sesame seeds, chilly, chopped shives, soja sauce, etc) available to your dish, which can make a difference. Overall the noodles are good. Then comes to the tempura... depending on their popularity, they might sit at the counter for I don’t know how long. The ones I got were cold and soggy...\nRead more\nWritten October 16, 2017",
